      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C20"],
      "claim": "Mebendazole, a benzimidazole carbamate, has very low absolute oral bioavailability (~1%) in humans; this is the main low-F concern, but its neutral benzimidazole scaffold is less transferable to the basic diaminopyrimidine query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C12"],
      "claim": "Flubendazole, another benzimidazole carbamate, shows low oral bioavailability in humans, but lacks the ionizable amino and fluorobenzyl features of the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "low",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because the query's diaminopyrimidine/carbamate/fluorobenzyl pharmacophore aligns with flupirtine and other kinase inhibitors with F > 20%, while the low-F benzimidazole carbamates are less transferable due to scaffold and ionization differences; the fed state may further aid absorption.",
